  "solution": "The pattern followed here is:\n\nWe have to interchange the two numbers to make the given equation correct.\n\nLet's check the option one by one.\n\n**Option 1) **6 and 8\n\nGiven : (6)2 – 20 + (28 ÷ 7) – [ {( {sqrt 4 } ) times 8} ] + (2)2 = 40\n\nAfter interchanging the numbers we get the:\n\n⇒ __**(8)**____**2**__ – 20 + __**(28 ÷ 7)**__ – [ {( {sqrt 4 } ) × 6} ]__** **__+ __**(2)**____**2**__ = 40\n\n⇒ 64 - 20 + 4 - __**2 × 6**__ + 4 = 40\n\n⇒ __**64**__ - 20 __**+ 4**__ - 12 __**+ 4 **__= 40\n\n⇒ __**72 - 20 - 12**__ = 40\n\n⇒ 40 = 40 \n\n⇒ **LHS = RHS**\n\n**Option 2) **7 and 2\n\nGiven : (6)2 – 20 + (28 ÷ 7) – [ {( {sqrt 4 } ) times 8} ] + (2)2 = 40\n\nAfter interchanging the numbers we get the:\n\n⇒ __**(6)**____**2**__ – 20 + __**(28 ÷ 2)**__ –** ****[ {( {sqrt 4 } ) × 8} ]**** **+ __**(7)**____**2**__ = 40\n\n⇒ 36 - 20 + 14 - __**2 × 8**__ + 49 = 40\n\n⇒ __**36**__ - 20 __**+ 14**__ - 16 __**+ 49**__ = 40\n\n⇒ 99 - 20 - 16 = 40\n\n⇒ 63 ≠ 40\n\n⇒ **LHS ≠ RHS**\n\n**Option 3) **2 and 8\n\nGiven : (6)2 – 20 + (28 ÷ 7) – [ {( {sqrt 4 } ) times 8} ] + (2)2 = 40\n\nAfter interchanging the numbers we get the:\n\n⇒ __**(6)**____**2**__ – 20 + __**(28 ÷ 7)**__ – [ {( {sqrt 4 } ) × 2} ] + __**(8)**____**2**____** **__= 40\n\n⇒ 36 - 20 + 4 - __**2 × 2**__ + 64 = 40\n\n⇒ __**36**__ - 20 __**+ 4**__ - 4 __**+ 64**__ = 40\n\n⇒ 104 - 20 - 4 = 40\n\n⇒ 80 ≠ 40\n\n⇒ **LHS ≠ RHS**\n\n**Option 4) **20 and 8\n\nGiven : (6)2 – 20 + (28 ÷ 7) – [ {( {sqrt 4 } ) times 8} ] + (2)2 = 40\n\nAfter interchanging the numbers we get the:\n\n⇒ __**(6)**____**2**__ – 8 + __**(28 ÷ 7)**__ – [ {( {sqrt 4 } ) × 20} ] + __**(2)**____**2**__ = 40\n\n⇒ 36 - 8 + 4 - **__2 × 20__** + 4 = 40\n\n⇒ __**36**__ - 8 __**+ 4**__ - 40 __**+ 4**__ = 40\n\n⇒ 44 - 8 - 40 = 40\n\n⇒ - 4 ≠ 40\n\n⇒ **LHS ≠ RHS**\n\nHence, the correct answer is **\"6 and 8\".**\n\n63",
